    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="gt_d41">

                <pb facs="gt_d41-1" n="1" xml:id="gt_d41-1"/>

                <head>GT–41. Telegram from the Ambassador in Guatemala (Muccio) to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="gt_d41-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Guatemala City</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-11-15T10:00:00-06:00">November 15, 1960,
                            10 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>228. Re Higdon telephone conversation last night, Foreign Minister said last
                    evening he instructing Alejos officially request U.S. armed forces assistance to
                    prevent within Guatemala air or sea-borne efforts introduce troops or supplies
                    to rebels. Said Alejos would communicate with Department as to exact wording GOG
                        request.<anchor n="2" xml:id="gt_d41-f2"/> Foreign Minister ecstatic about
                    U.S. willingness make this commitment, stating it was what GOG had long
                    wanted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Muccio</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
